<title>SINGAPORE: ST Energy has China power contract - Singapore TV.</title>
<headline>ST Energy has China power contract - Singapore TV.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Technologies Energy (ST Energy) has won a Singapore $400 million contract to build a power station in China's Chengdu, Singapore state television said in a report on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The report said that ST Energy would be involved in a joint venture with Szechuan Electric Power Corp to build the plant. ST Energy would have a 51 percent stake.</p>
<p>The plant will generate both electricity and industrial steam.</p>
<p>No further details were available and officials at ST Energy were unavailable for comment.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65) 870-3046</p>
</text>
